       See  the  NOTES  section for more information on scheduling classes and
       priorities, as well as the meaning of specifying _i_o_p_r_i_o as 0.

       I/O priorities are supported for reads and for  synchronous  (OO__DDIIRREECCTT,
       OO__SSYYNNCC)  writes.   I/O  priorities  are  not supported for asynchronous
       writes because they are issued  outside  the  context  of  the  program
       dirtying the memory, and thus program‐specific priorities do not apply.

